  "tools": [
   {
    "name": "dispatch",
    "description": "Prepare a chassis task card for a worker: writes the brief from the card, cuts the worktree (or, with here, shares the session's own checkout) and picks the tier, then returns the Agent call to make (a spawn block of JSON): the worker starts when you make it, and the mod records and verifies it. When every worker slot is taken it says queued, and tells you when a slot frees. Pass scope/forbid globs when the card's are prose. Pass repo, the absolute path of another local git checkout, for a task that works in that repo (a card written by the card tool with repo set to a path is found by its id alone). With verify (a sha), spawns nothing: runs the verifier on the work already in the task's worktree."
   },
   {
    "name": "verdict",
    "description": "Wait for a worker's verdict. When a background worker hands back, call this with its task id in that turn, before ending it: the verifier is still running, and this returns the verdict row (and any ready: line) as soon as it lands. If the verdict is already in it returns at once. If it is still verifying after waitSeconds it says so: call it again."
   },
   {
    "name": "card",
    "description": "When the person describes work to delegate, look at the repo to choose scope globs, then call this with the task (research or extraction with outputs outside the repo: repo none or here, scope = the output folder). For several workers at once pass lanes: one { title, scope } per worker, each with its own output folder, and put what the lanes share but none may touch (a notes file) in forbid; name a live app only one worker may use in resources, and the queue runs the lanes that hold it one at a time. It writes the card (one per lane), runs the dry run and returns the brief; show the person the summary and dispatch when they say go (call dispatch, or call this with dispatch: true when they already said to go ahead). Never ask the person to edit a card file."
   },
   {
    "name": "init",
    "description": "Scaffold chassis-delegation in this repo: a card folder (agents/tasks/, or docs/cards/ in a plugin repo) with its README and a sample card, .chassis-delegation.json with its defaults, and .delegation/ in .gitignore. Never overwrites a file; says what it wrote."
   },
   {
    "name": "setup",
    "description": "Checks the repo for chassis-delegation and returns what to fix; run the fixes, then call it again. When every required check holds it scaffolds the config and returns the first card to write."
   },
   {
    "name": "merge",
    "description": "After a consistent verdict with next=accept: rebases the task worktree onto the base, commits the card as merged, runs the card gates there, and returns the push/PR block to run verbatim. With finish: true, after the PR has landed: removes the root card, pulls, removes the worktree and branch, records the merge, and returns the remote cleanup (and release) lines. Never pushes and never calls gh itself."
   }
